+# Working with Rojo day to day
+
+Git is the source of truth for this game. `rojo serve` syncs the files in this repo into **your own
+dev place** in Studio. The dev place is a build of the repo. You don't author in it.
+
+## Setup (once)
+
+1. Install the tools with Rokit (`rokit install`). Use the `rojo` from `rokit.toml`, and make sure
+   the Rojo Studio plugin matches its version.
+2. Install packages: `pesde install` in the repo root, then again in `test_packages/`.
+3. Make your own dev place (a copy of the Baseplate is fine) and note its place id. Add that id to
+   `servePlaceIds` in `default.project.json` (create the array if it isn't there yet). Rojo then
+   refuses to live-sync into any other place, so a stray Connect can't overwrite a shared or live
+   place.
+
+## Daily loop
+
+1. `git pull` on your branch, with `rojo serve` stopped. Run `pesde install` again if `pesde.toml`
+   or `pesde.lock` changed.
+2. Start `rojo serve` from the repo root (port 34872, set by `servePort`). In Studio, open your dev
+   place and click **Connect** in the Rojo plugin.
+3. Edit files under `src/` in your editor. The README's Layout table shows where each folder lands
+   in the place. Name files by the scripts you want: `*.server.luau` makes a Script,
+   `*.client.luau` a LocalScript, and any other `.luau` a ModuleScript.
+4. Use Studio to read, run the Jest specs, and playtest. Don't make changes there.
+5. Before you commit, run the checks in the README (`rojo sourcemap`, `luau-lsp analyze`, `selene`,
+   `stylua --check`). Then read `git status` and `git diff`, and commit on your own branch.
+
+## Where changes go
+
+| Change | Where |
+|---|---|
+| Server code | `src/ServerScriptService` |
+| Code shared by server and client | `src/ReplicatedStorage/Shared` |
+| Client code | `src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts` |
+| UI | `src/StarterGui` |
+| Jest specs | `src/ServerScriptService/Tests/Specs` (`Name.spec.luau`) |
+| Attributes, tags, properties of a synced instance | A `Name.meta.json` beside the file (`init.meta.json` for a folder) |
+| A new package | `pesde.toml` (`test_packages/pesde.toml` for test-only packages), then `pesde install` |
+| Service settings, the Baseplate, a new mount | `default.project.json` (see below) |
+
+Never edit `roblox_packages/`, `test_packages/roblox_packages/`, or `sourcemap.json`. pesde and Rojo
+generate them, and the package files are hardlinked into a store that other projects share.
+Require packages through their links (`ReplicatedStorage.Packages.Vide`), never through a
+`.pesde/...` path.
+
+A script edited in Studio is overwritten by the next sync, and anything else changed there never
+reaches Git. If you truly need to build something in Studio (a model or a GUI), export it to an
+`.rbxm` in the repo, or use `rojo syncback` with `rojo serve` stopped. Then read the whole diff.
+
+## What to check while serving
+
+- **Did the change arrive?** After saving, open the script in Studio and confirm the new text is
+  there before you run a spec or a playtest. Otherwise you're testing the old code.
+- **Is `rojo serve` still running?** Rojo 7.7.0 and 7.7.1 crash when a file or folder is deleted,
+  moved, or renamed (`Rojo crashed!` in the terminal). Studio then silently stops getting changes.
+  Check the terminal after every delete or rename, or run `netstat -ano | findstr :34872`. If it
+  died, restart `rojo serve` and click Connect again.
+- **Stop `rojo serve` first** before `git checkout`, `switch`, `pull`, `rebase`, `reset`, `stash`, or
+  `clean`, before `pesde install`, and before deleting folders in bulk. Restart it afterward.
+- **Which code is the place running?** It runs whatever the connected server's folder has checked
+  out. A merged pull request isn't in your place until you pull it.
+- **Working on a second branch at the same time?** Use `git worktree add`, run `pesde install` in
+  the worktree, and serve it on its own port (`rojo serve --port 34873`).
+
+## Don't break `default.project.json`
+
+Every teammate's sync, sourcemap, and test run depends on this file. If it breaks, `rojo serve`
+and `rojo sourcemap` fail, or code lands in the wrong service. For example, Jest can't find
+`ServerScriptService.Tests.Packages`.
+
+- **The README's Layout table is the spec.** Change the table and the project file in the same
+  commit, and only on purpose.
+- **Know the non-obvious parts before touching them:**
+  - `globIgnorePaths` keeps `src/ServerScriptService/Tests` out of the automatic
+    `ServerScriptService` mount. The `Tests` node then mounts it explicitly, so it can also hold
+    `Packages` (the Jest packages from `test_packages/roblox_packages`). Removing either half
+    mounts `Tests` twice or loses the Jest packages.
+  - Jest packages belong under `ServerScriptService.Tests.Packages`, not in `ReplicatedStorage`.
+  - Every `$path` has to match a real folder name exactly (`StarterPlayerScripts`, with the `s`).
+- **Save it as UTF-8 without a BOM.** Rojo can't parse a project file that starts with a byte
+  order mark. Some editors and Windows PowerShell 5.1's `Set-Content` and `Out-File` add one. In
+  VS Code, check that the status bar says `UTF-8`, not `UTF-8 with BOM`.
+- **Resolving a merge conflict in it:** don't just pick one side. Merge both sides' intent, then
+  compare the result against the Layout table, entry by entry.
+- **Before committing a change to it,** run
+  `rojo sourcemap default.project.json -o sourcemap.json --include-non-scripts`. Then confirm that
+  `rojo serve` starts and that the specs still find `ServerScriptService.Tests.Packages.Jest`.
+- Ask for a review on any pull request that touches this file.
